  "worked_solution": "The surface area $S$ of a cube can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nS=6{s}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $s$ is the side length of the cube.\n\nSubstituting $s=2\\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{cm}$ into the formula, we get \n\n$$\nS=6(2\\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{cm})^{2}=120\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\n$$",
